import json
from pathlib import Path
w=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]
r=json.loads((w/'readers/scan007/record.json').read_text());r['scan']=7
for c in r['changes']:
    n=int(c['id'].split('-')[-1]);c['crop']=str(c['crop']).replace(str(w)+'/','')
    c['kind']='other'
    if n in {1,6,7,8,19,20,22,23,27,28,33,34,35,37,38,39,41,44,45,47}:c['kind']='misread word'
    if n in {3,4,9,10,11,43,48}:c['kind']='misread symbol or index'
    if n in {5,18}:c['kind']='insertion or placement'
    if n in {13,21,30,31,36,40,42,46}:c['kind']='abbreviation expanded or spelling modernised'
    if n in {14,24}:c['kind']='readable ink left as \\ill{}'
    if n in {15,16}:c['kind']='deletion state (struck given live or live given struck)'
    if n in {25,26,32}:c['kind']='omission'
    if n in {6,7,15,18,19,21}:c['against_c']=False
    if n==11:
        c['final']=r'$u_{\omega}$';c['against_c']=True;c['against_h']=False;c['confidence']='high'
        c['evidence']+=' Main-reader decision: the two rounded bowls, interior rise and upturned right tip match the locally established omega on scan006. The whole u-subscript expression is resolved to u_omega on this crop.'
        c['math_note']='The shared notation and matching two-bowl form resolve the subscript as omega; no alteration to the claimed action is made.'
r['changes']=[c for c in r['changes'] if c['id'] not in {'scan007-15','scan007-49'}]
r['doubts']=[d for d in r['doubts'] if d['place']!='Subscript on u in the opening paragraph']
for b in r['second_boxes']:b['reading']=b['reading'].replace(r'u_{\unsure{\omega|w}}',r'u_{\omega}')
for i in r['inventory']:
    i['sheet_kind']='text';i['hand']='another unnamed hand (archive numeral)' if 'Archival' in i['element'] else 'his hand'
r['notation']=[s.replace('The action variable is u_{\\omega|w}; the two-bowl subscript remains unresolved.','The action variable is u_omega; the two rounded bowls and raised outer tip match the omega established on scan006.') for s in r['notation']]
r['notes']=[
 'The opening continuation says that a connected oriented contour amounts to an integer n≥2 and a torsor under Z/nZ. It gives cyclic-group, inverse-generator-pair and torsor data for a connected contour, then explicitly qualifies this by n≥3 and replaces the inverse pair with an abstract two-element set Ω mapping to G. The lower remark identifies an oriented contour, not necessarily connected, with a set carrying a Z-action; the unoriented counterpart stops after an ellipsis. No date or author page number is present; the pencil 6 is archival.',
 'The source starts with connexe, not H’s Contour. It writes a two-stroke equality in “revient au =”, the abbreviation gpe, and singular Contour/ensemble/lequel in the lower remark. The above-line tel and the small cardinality parenthesis are insertions. The cancellation after partie reaches through d-apostrophe. The long line under the beginning of générateur is the returning g descender, not underlining. The final marks after equality are an unfinished ellipsis, not un.',
 'The first circular superscript of G remains 0/circle, and its repeated notation uses the first candidate. The map label sigma/r, the flattened ou/au versus dash-like marks, cancelled ens/un and sinon/si on, and the lower variable u/n remain doubtful. The two rounded lobes of the u subscript match the established omega on scan006, settling that local doubt. The source writes bare G in item 2 bis; the superscript 0 is not supplied from context. Its opening parenthesis remains unmatched.',
 'Targeted check: in a cyclic group generated by g of finite order n≥2, g=g⁻¹ exactly when g²=1, hence exactly when n=2. Thus the stated inverse-generator pair has cardinal two precisely for n≠2; replacing the pair by an abstract two-element set avoids its collapse when n=2. The ink’s doubtful abbreviation sss/ss/ssi is retained despite the mathematical equivalence.',
 'Two qualifications are needed if the claims are read with the earlier loopless-contour definition. The doubly infinite path from scan005 requires the infinite cyclic group, which is absent from the opening n∈N, n≥2 description unless that sentence is limited to finite contours. Also an arbitrary Z-action may have fixed points: a singleton with the identity action would create a loop, disallowed by two distinct endpoints per edge. For loopless oriented contours the corresponding permutation must have no fixed points; its orbits then give cycles of length at least two or doubly infinite paths. These are notes on the claims, not supplied restrictions in the transcription.'
]
r['check_events']=[
 {'statement_id':'scan007-generator-pair','type':'targeted proof check','outcome':'For a generator of finite order n≥2, g=g⁻¹ iff g²=1 iff n=2. The pair therefore has cardinal 2 iff n≠2, and an abstract two-element Ω retains two labels at n=2.'},
 {'statement_id':'scan007-Z-action-description','type':'refuted, with the refined statement\'s id','outcome':'The unrestricted description includes the identity action on a singleton, which would require a loop under the preceding two-distinct-endpoints definition. Refined statement scan007-fixed-point-free-action: fixed-point-free permutations give loopless oriented contours, with finite orbits of length ≥2 or infinite cyclic orbits. The initial finite n description also needs a finite-contour restriction or an infinite-cyclic case.'}
]
r['root_review']='Main reader inspected the whole scan and all 50 returned evidence crops. The omega subscript was resolved by its crop and the established local glyph form. Other open places retain the stated alternatives. Pure added doubt is not counted as a C text change; the archive marker is kept in inventory rather than as a macro-only collation row.'
r['review_date']='2026-11-20';r['crop_count']=50
(w/'records/scan007.json').write_text(json.dumps(r,ensure_ascii=False,indent=2))
(w/'pages/J75-01_75_scan007.tex').write_text((w/'readers/scan007/proposal.tex').read_text().replace(r'u_{\unsure{\omega|w}}',r'u_{\omega}'))
with (w/'notation.md').open('a') as f:
    f.write('\n- Scan 007: `u_omega` has the same two rounded omega bowls as scan006 and is resolved consistently. `G^{0|circle}` remains graphically doubtful at its first occurrence; repeated local notation uses 0. The source switches to bare G in item 2 bis. The abbreviations `gpe`, `ens`, `gén.`, `néc./néc` and `autom` retain their individual punctuation.\n')
print('approved',r['scan'],len(r['changes']))
